<dl class="readouts">
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Temperature</dt>
        <dd>@TemperatureText</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Absorbed sunlight</dt>
        <dd>@FluxText(Budget.Absorbed)</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Heat to space</dt>
        <dd>@FluxText(Budget.HeatToSpace)</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Imbalance</dt>
        <dd>@FluxText(Budget.Imbalance, signed: true)</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Total forcing</dt>
        <dd>@FluxText(Forcing.Total, signed: true)</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="readout">
        <dt>Warming per doubling of CO₂</dt>
        <dd>@PerDoublingText</dd>
    </div>
</dl>
<p class="note">
    The imbalance is the absorbed sunlight less the heat to space. It stays small, because the planet warms until the
    heat it sends to space catches up with the forcing.
</p>
